1
00:00:00,012 --> 00:00:02,352
(Sheldon:)Right. Always right.

2
00:00:02,349 --> 00:00:03,649
(Howard:)He's a righty.

3
00:00:03,650 --> 00:00:06,220
(Penny:)Okay,

4
00:00:06,219 --> 00:00:07,319
(Barry:)show me en garde.

5
00:00:07,320 --> 00:00:09,650
(Barry:)Good. Knees bent,

6
00:00:09,656 --> 00:00:11,326
slightly over the toe.

7
00:00:11,324 --> 00:00:14,024
Non-sword hand up for balance.

8
00:00:14,027 --> 00:00:17,997
(groans) I am going
to feel this tomorrow.

9
00:00:17,997 --> 00:00:21,197
(Barry:)The first move
is called an advance.

10
00:00:21,201 --> 00:00:23,671
You move your front foot
forward, heel to toe.

11
00:00:23,670 --> 00:00:25,670
(Barry:)Back foot
follows.

12
00:00:25,672 --> 00:00:28,072
So front foot forward,
heel to toe.

13
00:00:28,074 --> 00:00:29,804
Back foot follows.

14
00:00:29,809 --> 00:00:32,479
Now you try. Advance.

15
00:00:32,478 --> 00:00:36,048
(Barry:)And advance.
And advance.

16
00:00:36,049 --> 00:00:39,419
(Leonard:)This is easy.
I didn't need to wear a cup.

17
00:00:39,419 --> 00:00:40,449
KRIPKE:
Good.

18
00:00:40,453 --> 00:00:42,223
(Barry:)The next move is called
a retreat.

19
00:00:42,221 --> 00:00:43,321
(Barry:)Step back.

20
00:00:43,322 --> 00:00:45,322
(Barry:)Back foot first, toe to heel.

21
00:00:45,324 --> 00:00:46,994
Front foot follows.

22
00:00:46,993 --> 00:00:48,623
(Sheldon:)On three.

23
00:00:48,628 --> 00:00:49,858
(Sheldon:)Excuse me, Barry?
Yes.

24
00:00:49,862 --> 00:00:52,232
(Sheldon:)When can I stab
one of my friends?

25
00:00:53,365 --> 00:00:55,095
(Barry:)In fencing,
we don't call it a stab.

26
00:00:55,101 --> 00:00:56,871
(Barry:)We call it a touch.
Uh, yes, I'm aware.

27
00:00:56,869 --> 00:00:58,739
(Sheldon:)But if I say I want
to touch one of my friends,

